      "source": [
        "## 7. Scaling note\n",
        "\n",
        "**Running it.** Run `run_agent.py` in a container as a daily scheduled job (Cloud Scheduler → Cloud Run Job, or EventBridge → ECS), after the day's ad data lands. Read the data from the warehouse instead of a CSV, and keep yesterday's allocation in a database. Each plan is written with an idempotency key (account + date), so a re-run never applies twice. Start in dry-run mode, where a human approves each plan. API keys live in a secret manager.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Retries and fallbacks.** Gemini calls use SDK retries with exponential backoff (5 attempts, covering 429 rate limits and 5xx errors), a 120-second timeout, and a backup model if the default model isn't available. If Gemini still fails, the agent uses the rule-based policy. If the data is stale or missing, it keeps yesterday's split. Ad-platform writes are retried. Failures go to a dead-letter queue and raise an alert, and a plan is applied all at once or not at all.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Monitoring and logging.** Ship the JSON logs (`run_log.jsonl`: run ID, allocation, policy, fallbacks, tokens) to Cloud Logging or CloudWatch. Keep `decision_log.csv` as the audit trail. A dashboard tracks CPA and conversions against a **live holdout** (about 10% of budget on a fixed split), how often guardrails fire, the fallback rate, and LLM cost. Alerts go off when a run fails, data is late, CPA jumps more than 30%, or fallbacks become frequent.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Cost controls.**\n",
        "- *Ad spend:* the code enforces the exact daily total and the ±20% limit, and campaign caps on the ad platform act as a second line of defense.\n",
        "- *LLM:* one short conversation per account per day, at most 4 turns, a token budget per run, a Flash-tier model by default, an adjustable thinking level, context caching, and the Gemini Batch API (about 50% cheaper) for many accounts.\n",
        "- *Cloud:* jobs scale to zero between runs, and billing alerts are on."
      ]
